  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme Pathway 3 (ACRS P3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project provides comprehensive resettlement support to 1,300 beneficiaries identified by the Government of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland (UK) for resettlement to the UK. The caseload consists of eligible beneficiaries, including British Council contractors, GardaWorld contractors and Chevening alumni, specifically from the Islamic Republic of Pakistan (1,000), and an unallocated caseload of approximately 300 beneficiaries from unspecified locations. IOM will facilitate video/telephone interviewing to assess beneficiaries&#x2019; accommodation needs in relation to local authority availability, provide pre-migration health activities including the early identification of children&#x2019;s Special Educational Needs (SEN) and the application of the Global Mental Health Assessment tool (GMHAT) for adult beneficiaries in agreed Missions,  pre-embarkation checks, 3-day pre-departure orientation (UKCO) sessions, visa/travel document processing, movement management and operational support to the final destination, including operational and/or medical escorts if requested and the delivery of information sessions to Local Authorities and other relevant resettlement stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
